\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou Judges of quick and dead,
\par Before whose bar severe,
\par With holy joy, or guilty dread,
\par We all shall soon appear:
\par Our cautioned souls prepare
\par For that tremendous day,
\par And fill us now with watchful care,
\par And stir us up to pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. To pray, and wait the hour,
\par That awful hour unknown,
\par When, robed in majesty and power,
\par Thou shalt from heaven come down,
\par The immortal Son of Man,
\par To judge the human race,
\par With all their Father's dazzling,
\par With all Thy glorious grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O may we thus be found
\par Obedient to His word,
\par Attentive to the trumpet's sound,
\par And looking for our Lord.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O may we thus ensure
\par A lot among the blest;
\par And watch a moment to secure
\par An everlasting rest.
\par                          Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

